# Git submodules
#
# paths below are prefixed with **/ because this ignore file lives at
# .config/prettier/, and gitignore anchoring resolves any pattern
# containing a non-trailing / relative to the ignore file's own
# directory, not the repo root -- an unprefixed path here would silently
# never match
**/home/.hammerspoon/Spoons/ControlEscape.spoon
**/vendor/vim-pathogen
**/vendor/vim-plug
**/vendor/sbp
**/config/cheat/cheatsheets/community
**/config/cheat/cheatsheets/personal

# automatically pulled
**/home/.vim/plugged

# stuff that doesn't need formatting
**/config/fish/fish_plugins

# auto-generated issue-tracker files (beans); change constantly and contain
# markdown-emphasis-like text (*, _) that prettier rewrites, breaking CI on
# every push. Not hand-authored, so don't lint them.
.beans/

# stuff without prettier support
*.fish
.editorconfig
**/home/.gitconfig
**/config/ghostty/config

# live app data, not hand-authored -- Karabiner-Elements rewrites this file
# in place (4-space indent) whenever its settings change, since
# ~/.config/karabiner is symlinked straight to this repo path
**/karabiner/karabiner.json

# same idea, one step removed: this is a copy of what ccstatusline itself
# writes to ~/.config/ccstatusline (not symlinked, copied in by hand after
# changing the status line). prettier wants single-element arrays collapsed
# onto one line, the tool writes them expanded, so the file goes
# out-of-format again every time it is refreshed. It had CI red on main for
# days before anyone tied the failure to it.
**/config/ccstatusline/settings.json
